        "text": "Coordination final exam note: A complete answer should separate detection, transmission, integration and response. Receptors detect a change, neural or hormonal pathways carry information, coordinating centres determine an appropriate response, and effectors produce the action. When a question compares nervous and hormonal coordination, use the same criteria on both sides: nature of signal, route, speed, duration and examples. This makes the comparison balanced and prevents vague statements. Case-based questions are usually solved by identifying the first stimulus and then tracing the pathway forward until the final response. The same reasoning works for reflex action, plant tropism and endocrine regulation even though the structures involved are different."
